# Server — Express API

## Architecture (MVC + services)

```text
app.js          → middleware + mount routers only (keep minimal)
routes/index.js → register all routers → app.use('/api', routes)
controllers/    → thin: req/res handling only
services/       → business logic, framework-agnostic
models/         → Mongoose schemas (lowercase model names/refs)
middleware/     → auth, error, upload, validate
```

## Conventions

- **ES Modules** with `.js` extension in relative imports:
  `import connectDB from './config/db.js'`
- **async/await** everywhere; thin controllers — logic lives in `services/`.
- Register routers in `routes/index.js`, never directly in `app.js`.
- Mongoose refs use lowercase names: `'user'`, `'category'`, `'recipe'`.
- Add indexes for fields used in frequent queries.

## Example — thin controller

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD — delegate to service
export async function listRecipes(req, res, next) {
  try {
    const recipes = await recipeService.listByUser(req.userId);
    res.json({ success: true, data: recipes });
  } catch (err) {
    next(err);
  }
}
```

## Commands

```bash
cd server && npm run dev   # http://localhost:5000
```

Verify the app boots before proposing a merge.
